<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kriegman et al. (2020) Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuation & Passive Ectoderm Volume Invariance Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs rhythmic volumetric actuation of contractile cardiac voxels while enforcing strict rest-volume invariance in passive animal-cap ectoderm voxels | Variables: L_{ij,0}: rest spring length between adjacent voxels; a_{ij} in {0,1}: tissue type (0 = passive ectoderm, 1 = contractile cardiac progenitor); epsilon_act = 0.18: volumetric contraction strain; f_act = 1.5 Hz: cardiac contraction frequency" ;
    dct:source "Kriegman, Blackiston, Levin & Bongard (2020) PNAS 117(4):1853-1859 SI Appendix S1; Cheney et al. (2013) GECCO pp. 167-174" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py#L170-L271>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean#L14-L39> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def voxel_rest_length (L0 a eps s : Int) : Int :=
  L0 + a * eps * s
theorem voxel_actuation_invariance_and_cycle_symmetry (L0 a eps s : Int) :
    voxel_rest_length L0 0 eps s = L0 ∧
    voxel_rest_length L0 a 0 s = L0 ∧
    voxel_rest_length L0 1 eps s + voxel_rest_length L0 1 eps (-s) = 2 * L0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · simp [voxel_rest_length]
  · simp [voxel_rest_length]
  · simp [voxel_rest_length, Int.mul_neg]
    omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L_{ij}(t) = L_{ij,0}(1 + ε_act a_{ij} sin(ω t + φ_{ij}));   a_{ij}=0 ⟹ L_{ij}(t)=L_{ij,0};   L_{ij}(+s)+L_{ij}(-s)=2L_{ij,0}" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1910837117>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112672118>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.abf1571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463404> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuated Continuum Mechanics, Age-Fitness Pareto Optimization (AFPO), & Kinematic Self-Replication" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.voxel_rest_length" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.voxel_actuation_invariance_and_cycle_symmetry" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Ventral-Concavity Asymmetric Substrate Ratchet & Dorsal Inversion Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that ventral-concavity bipedal leg asymmetry rectifies zero-mean cardiac oscillations into net forward locomotion, whereas 180-deg dorsal inversion equalizes contact friction and collapses net propulsion | Variables: mu_ant = 0.65: anterior ventral leg substrate friction; mu_post = 0.18: posterior ventral leg substrate friction; e: cyclic ventral cardiac contraction stroke" ;
    dct:source "Kriegman, Blackiston, Levin & Bongard (2020) PNAS 117(4):1853-1859 Figs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py#L274-L415>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean#L42-L68> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def xenobot_stride (mu_ant mu_post e : Int) : Int :=
  (mu_ant - mu_post) * e
theorem ventral_ratchet_and_dorsal_inversion_collapse (mu mu_ant mu_post e : Int) :
    xenobot_stride mu mu e = 0 ∧
    xenobot_stride mu_post mu_ant e = -xenobot_stride mu_ant mu_post e ∧
    xenobot_stride 65 18 4 = 188 ∧
    xenobot_stride 25 25 4 = 0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [xenobot_stride]
  · simp [xenobot_stride, Int.sub_mul]
    omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δx_stride(μ_ant, μ_post, e) = (μ_ant - μ_post) e;   μ_ant = μ_post ⟹ Δx_stride = 0;   Δx_stride(μ_post, μ_ant, e) = -Δx_stride(μ_ant, μ_post, e)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1910837117>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112672118>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.abf1571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463404> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuated Continuum Mechanics, Age-Fitness Pareto Optimization (AFPO), & Kinematic Self-Replication" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.xenobot_stride" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.ventral_ratchet_and_dorsal_inversion_collapse" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "AFPO Phase-Robustness Transferability & Pac-Man Kinematic Self-Replication Law" ;
    dct:description "Formalizes the Kriegman et al. (2020) phase-randomization sim-to-real transferability filter and the Kriegman et al. (2021) C-shaped Pac-Man kinematic self-replication advantage over spherical morphologies | Variables: F_det: synchronous cardiac phase displacement (body lengths); F_rob: phase-randomized cardiomyocyte displacement; eta_mouth(theta_mouth): C-shaped Pac-Man concavity sweeping efficiency; N_thresh = 55: critical stem-cell pile size for self-sustaining daughter spheroid compaction" ;
    dct:source "Kriegman et al. (2020) PNAS 117:1853-1859 Fig. 2; Kriegman et al. (2021) PNAS 118:e2112672118 Figs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py#L417-L536>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean#L71-L100> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def afpo_transferable (F_det F_rob F_det_min F_rob_min : Nat) : Bool :=
  (F_det ≥ F_det_min) && (F_rob ≥ F_rob_min)
def kinematic_daughter_generations (eta_mouth v_orbit rho_free N_thresh : Nat) : Nat :=
  (eta_mouth * v_orbit * rho_free) / N_thresh
theorem afpo_transferability_and_pacman_replication :
    afpo_transferable 195 140 120 100 = true ∧
    afpo_transferable 185 32 120 100 = false ∧
    afpo_transferable 12 10 120 100 = false ∧
    kinematic_daughter_generations 18 3 4 55 = 3 ∧
    kinematic_daughter_generations 6 3 4 55 = 1 := by
  decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T_sim2real(F_det, F_rob) = I(F_det ≥ F_min ∧ F_rob ≥ F_rob_min);   N_daughters(θ_mouth) = floor(η_sweep(θ_mouth) v_orbit ρ_free / N_thresh)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1910837117>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112672118>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.abf1571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463404> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuated Continuum Mechanics, Age-Fitness Pareto Optimization (AFPO), & Kinematic Self-Replication" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.kinematic_daughter_generations" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.afpo_transferability_and_pacman_replication" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Regularised-Stokeslet Force-Free Cancellation & Squirmer Mobility Superposition Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees that the force-free squirmer flow has no net-Stokeslet (log) far field and that the mobility is affine in the turn bias, which is how the orbit radius is fitted and the precessing orbit is driven without re-solving the boundary integral | Variables: f_k: regularised Stokeslet strengths on the parent boundary; c: the common scalar part of the 2D kernel (-(1/2) constant and far-field -ln r); U0, U1: rigid velocity at zero and unit left/right ciliary turn bias; beta: turn bias" ;
    dct:source "Cortez (2001) SIAM J. Sci. Comput. 23:1204-1225 (regularised Stokeslets); Blake (1971) J. Fluid Mech. 46:199-208 (squirmer); Kriegman et al. (2021) PNAS 118:e2112672118" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py#L923-L1080>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean#L101-L135> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def stokeslet_constant_part (c f1 f2 f3 : Int) : Int :=
  c * f1 + c * f2 + c * f3
def squirmer_velocity (U0 U1 beta : Int) : Int :=
  U0 + beta * U1
theorem stokeslet_force_free_cancellation_and_mobility_superposition
    (c f1 f2 f3 U0 U1 b1 b2 : Int) (hff : f1 + f2 + f3 = 0) :
    stokeslet_constant_part c f1 f2 f3 = 0 ∧
    squirmer_velocity U0 U1 0 = U0 ∧
    squirmer_velocity U0 U1 1 = U0 + U1 ∧
    squirmer_velocity U0 U1 (b1 + b2) = squirmer_velocity U0 U1 b1 + b2 * U1 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · unfold stokeslet_constant_part
    rw [← Int.mul_add, ← Int.mul_add, hff, Int.mul_zero]
  · simp [squirmer_velocity]
  · simp [squirmer_velocity]
  · simp [squirmer_velocity, Int.add_mul]
    omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Σ_k c f_k = c Σ_k f_k = 0 for a force-free body;   U(β) = U0 + β U1,  U(β₁+β₂) = U(β₁) + β₂ U1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1910837117>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112672118>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.abf1571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463404> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuated Continuum Mechanics, Age-Fitness Pareto Optimization (AFPO), & Kinematic Self-Replication" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.squirmer_velocity" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.stokeslet_force_free_cancellation_and_mobility_superposition" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "3D Voxel Lattice Stokes-Drag Dissipation & Passive-Spring Rest Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Explains the monotone fitness decrease with Stokes drag (gamma in {0,1,2,4,8}) and the zero locomotion of the passive_only_control body in the 8x8x7 lattice | Variables: gamma: per-node Stokes drag coefficient (non-dimensional, default 2.0); v: node velocity; L_ij,0: spring rest length; a_ij: fraction of cardiac voxels adjoining the spring (0 for passive-only springs)" ;
    dct:source "Kriegman, Blackiston, Levin & Bongard (2020) PNAS 117(4):1853-1859 SI Appendix S1 (VoxCAD 8x8x7 workspace); Hiller & Lipson (2014) Soft Robotics 1:88-101 (VoxCAD dynamics)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py#L674-L917>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean#L138-L166> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def drag_power (gamma v : Int) : Int :=
  gamma * (v * v)
theorem int_mul_self_nonneg (v : Int) : 0 ≤ v * v := by
  rcases Int.le_total 0 v with h | h
  · exact Int.mul_nonneg h h
  · have h' : 0 ≤ -v := Int.neg_nonneg_of_nonpos h
    have hm := Int.mul_nonneg h' h'
    rwa [Int.neg_mul_neg] at hm
theorem lattice_drag_dissipation_nonneg_and_passive_spring_rest
    (gamma v L0 eps s : Int) (hg : 0 ≤ gamma) :
    0 ≤ drag_power gamma v ∧
    drag_power 0 v = 0 ∧
    voxel_rest_length L0 0 eps s = L0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact Int.mul_nonneg hg (int_mul_self_nonneg v)
  · simp [drag_power]
  · simp [voxel_rest_length]
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_drag = γ v·v ≥ 0 for γ ≥ 0;   P_drag(γ=0) = 0;   a_ij = 0 ⟹ L_ij(t) = L_ij,0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1910837117>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112672118>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.abf1571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463404> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuated Continuum Mechanics, Age-Fitness Pareto Optimization (AFPO), & Kinematic Self-Replication" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.drag_power" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.lattice_drag_dissipation_nonneg_and_passive_spring_rest" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form" ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-3> .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kriegman et al. (2020) Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuation & Passive Ectoderm Volume Invariance Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs rhythmic volumetric actuation of contractile cardiac voxels while enforcing strict rest-volume invariance in passive animal-cap ectoderm voxels | Variables: L_{ij,0}: rest spring length between adjacent voxels; a_{ij} in {0,1}: tissue type (0 = passive ectoderm, 1 = contractile cardiac progenitor); epsilon_act = 0.18: volumetric contraction strain; f_act = 1.5 Hz: cardiac contraction frequency" ;
    dct:source "Kriegman, Blackiston, Levin & Bongard (2020) PNAS 117(4):1853-1859 SI Appendix S1; Cheney et al. (2013) GECCO pp. 167-174" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py#L125-L215>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean#L14-L39> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def voxel_rest_length (L0 a eps s : Int) : Int :=
  L0 + a * eps * s
theorem voxel_actuation_invariance_and_cycle_symmetry (L0 a eps s : Int) :
    voxel_rest_length L0 0 eps s = L0 ∧
    voxel_rest_length L0 a 0 s = L0 ∧
    voxel_rest_length L0 1 eps s + voxel_rest_length L0 1 eps (-s) = 2 * L0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · simp [voxel_rest_length]
  · simp [voxel_rest_length]
  · simp [voxel_rest_length, Int.mul_neg]
    omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L_{ij}(t) = L_{ij,0}(1 + ε_act a_{ij} sin(ω t + φ_{ij}));   a_{ij}=0 ⟹ L_{ij}(t)=L_{ij,0};   L_{ij}(+s)+L_{ij}(-s)=2L_{ij,0}" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1910837117>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112672118>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.abf1571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463404> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuated Continuum Mechanics, Age-Fitness Pareto Optimization (AFPO), & Kinematic Self-Replication" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.voxel_rest_length" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.voxel_actuation_invariance_and_cycle_symmetry" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Ventral-Concavity Asymmetric Substrate Ratchet & Dorsal Inversion Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that ventral-concavity bipedal leg asymmetry rectifies zero-mean cardiac oscillations into net forward locomotion, whereas 180-deg dorsal inversion equalizes contact friction and collapses net propulsion | Variables: mu_ant = 0.65: anterior ventral leg substrate friction; mu_post = 0.18: posterior ventral leg substrate friction; e: cyclic ventral cardiac contraction stroke" ;
    dct:source "Kriegman, Blackiston, Levin & Bongard (2020) PNAS 117(4):1853-1859 Figs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py#L220-L360>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean#L42-L68> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def xenobot_stride (mu_ant mu_post e : Int) : Int :=
  (mu_ant - mu_post) * e
theorem ventral_ratchet_and_dorsal_inversion_collapse (mu mu_ant mu_post e : Int) :
    xenobot_stride mu mu e = 0 ∧
    xenobot_stride mu_post mu_ant e = -xenobot_stride mu_ant mu_post e ∧
    xenobot_stride 65 18 4 = 188 ∧
    xenobot_stride 25 25 4 = 0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [xenobot_stride]
  · simp [xenobot_stride, Int.sub_mul]
    omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δx_stride(μ_ant, μ_post, e) = (μ_ant - μ_post) e;   μ_ant = μ_post ⟹ Δx_stride = 0;   Δx_stride(μ_post, μ_ant, e) = -Δx_stride(μ_ant, μ_post, e)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1910837117>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112672118>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.abf1571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463404> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuated Continuum Mechanics, Age-Fitness Pareto Optimization (AFPO), & Kinematic Self-Replication" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.xenobot_stride" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.ventral_ratchet_and_dorsal_inversion_collapse" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "AFPO Phase-Robustness Transferability & Pac-Man Kinematic Self-Replication Law" ;
    dct:description "Formalizes the Kriegman et al. (2020) phase-randomization sim-to-real transferability filter and the Kriegman et al. (2021) C-shaped Pac-Man kinematic self-replication advantage over spherical morphologies | Variables: F_det: synchronous cardiac phase displacement (body lengths); F_rob: phase-randomized cardiomyocyte displacement; eta_mouth(theta_mouth): C-shaped Pac-Man concavity sweeping efficiency; N_thresh = 55: critical stem-cell pile size for self-sustaining daughter spheroid compaction" ;
    dct:source "Kriegman et al. (2020) PNAS 117:1853-1859 Fig. 2; Kriegman et al. (2021) PNAS 118:e2112672118 Figs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py#L365-L520>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean#L71-L100> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def afpo_transferable (F_det F_rob F_det_min F_rob_min : Nat) : Bool :=
  (F_det ≥ F_det_min) && (F_rob ≥ F_rob_min)
def kinematic_daughter_generations (eta_mouth v_orbit rho_free N_thresh : Nat) : Nat :=
  (eta_mouth * v_orbit * rho_free) / N_thresh
theorem afpo_transferability_and_pacman_replication :
    afpo_transferable 195 140 120 100 = true ∧
    afpo_transferable 185 32 120 100 = false ∧
    afpo_transferable 12 10 120 100 = false ∧
    kinematic_daughter_generations 18 3 4 55 = 3 ∧
    kinematic_daughter_generations 6 3 4 55 = 1 := by
  decide
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T_sim2real(F_det, F_rob) = I(F_det ≥ F_min ∧ F_rob ≥ F_rob_min);   N_daughters(θ_mouth) = floor(η_sweep(θ_mouth) v_orbit ρ_free / N_thresh)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1910837117>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112672118>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.abf1571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463404> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Voxel Spring-Lattice Actuated Continuum Mechanics, Age-Fitness Pareto Optimization (AFPO), & Kinematic Self-Replication" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_083.kinematic_daughter_generations" ;
